# MAGIC ### Problem Statement
# MAGIC The current financial statement tie-out process relies heavily on manual effort. The audit team must identify the GL accounts supporting each disclosure line item, apply grouping-code mappings, aggregate balances, and compare the calculated amounts with the financial statements.
# MAGIC Although ANA-007 supports this process, maintaining grouping-code assignments and updating disclosures remains manual. As the number of disclosures and mapped accounts increases, the process becomes repetitive, time-consuming, and more susceptible to mapping errors, inconsistent updates, and incomplete documentation.
# MAGIC The proposed tool will automate and standardize the tie-out process using predefined mappings between GL accounts, grouping codes, and financial statement disclosure line items. This will improve efficiency, consistency, accuracy, and traceability.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Process Followed to Resolve the Issue
# MAGIC - Identify the GL trial balance, grouping codes, financial statement line items, disclosure data, and reporting-period information required for the tie-out.
# MAGIC - Create and maintain predefined relationships between GL accounts, grouping codes, and financial statement disclosure line items.
# MAGIC - Import the trial balance and disclosure data, then perform checks for missing fields, invalid grouping codes, duplicate accounts, and inconsistent mappings.
# MAGIC - Use the approved grouping-code mappings to automatically aggregate GL balances for each financial statement line item.
# MAGIC - Compare the calculated balances with the amounts presented in the financial statements and identify any differences.
# MAGIC - Produce a clear list of unmapped accounts, missing disclosure lines, balance variances, and other items requiring investigation.
# MAGIC - Generate a repeatable tie-out output that includes mappings, calculations, results, exceptions, and review-ready supporting information.
